#: ../../source/chapters/08-superpowers.md:7 4ebe44bdff714c8583dac0231b3ca4ac
msgid "Case Study: Superpowers"
msgstr "案例研究：Superpowers"

#: ../../source/chapters/08-superpowers.md:9 4641a1d5e3034e4581b00a3e737a9219
msgid ""
"*Not a framework. Not a platform. A library of skills that teach the agent "
"how to think twice before it writes.*"
msgstr "*不是框架，不是平台。是一整套技能（skills），教智能体在动笔之前先想两遍。*"

#: ../../source/chapters/08-superpowers.md:11 81b9f125a5d9452ea3cb9e5914b539c8
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Superpowers, authored by Joseph Vincent and released as open source under "
"the `obra/superpowers` repository "
"{cite}`vincent2025superpowers,vincent2025superpowersrepo`, is the "
"philosophical opposite of OpenHarness: where OpenHarness ships a runtime and"
" a sandbox, Superpowers ships *only* a set of `SKILL.md` files that "
"structure *how* an agent (specifically, Claude Code) frames its own work. "
"The whole project is essentially three dozen markdown files. That is the "
"point."
msgstr ""
"Superpowers 由 Joseph Vincent 编写，以 `obra/superpowers` 仓库开源发布 "
"{cite}`vincent2025superpowers,vincent2025superpowersrepo`。它在哲学上是 OpenHarness"
" 的反面：OpenHarness 交付的是运行时和沙箱，Superpowers 交付的 *只是* 一组 `SKILL.md` "
"文件，用来塑造一个智能体（具体说是 Claude Code）\"如何框自己的工作\"。整个项目本质上就是三十来份 markdown "
"文件——这本身，就是它的论点。"

#: ../../source/chapters/08-superpowers.md:19 1c7fd28ab9614be999593d6f860c1a2b
msgid "§08.1 — Skills-first workflow"
msgstr "§08.1 —— 以技能为先的工作流"

#: ../../source/chapters/08-superpowers.md:21 e07ef0787b3540958173d08dce3723ee
msgid "The canonical Superpowers workflow is a five-step arc:"
msgstr "Superpowers 的经典工作流是一条五步弧："

#: ../../source/chapters/08-superpowers.md:23 959daffadef2441fb9cf8e9ea37d88fa
msgid ""
"**Brainstorming** (`skills/brainstorming/SKILL.md`) — refuse to implement "
"until intent is clarified."
msgstr "**头脑风暴**（`skills/brainstorming/SKILL.md`）—— 在意图被澄清之前，拒绝开始实现。"

#: ../../source/chapters/08-superpowers.md:25 d5a20d38c67648ec93375d0d532919e5
msgid ""
"**Writing plans** (`skills/writing-plans/SKILL.md`) — compile the brainstorm"
" into a written plan with review checkpoints."
msgstr "**写计划**（`skills/writing-plans/SKILL.md`）—— 把头脑风暴编译成一份带评审节点的书面计划。"

#: ../../source/chapters/08-superpowers.md:27 a00eac6bcaae4a99b582cc4523c335f5
msgid ""
"**Test-driven development** (`skills/test-driven-development/SKILL.md`) — "
"implement only against a failing test."
msgstr ""
"**测试驱动开发**（`skills/test-driven-development/SKILL.md`）—— 只对着一条失败的测试来实现。"

#: ../../source/chapters/08-superpowers.md:29 a7adda8678d449f0a093352d65b6f440
msgid ""
"**Code review** (`skills/requesting-code-review/SKILL.md`) — explicit review"
" with named rubric before merging."
msgstr ""
"**代码评审**（`skills/requesting-code-review/SKILL.md`）—— 合并之前，进行一次带有明确评价细则的显式评审。"

#: ../../source/chapters/08-superpowers.md:31 583af3bcfdef4574a7d03793cf047545
msgid ""
"**Finishing** (`skills/finishing-a-development-branch/SKILL.md`) — "
"integration, cleanup, PR."
msgstr ""
"**收尾**（`skills/finishing-a-development-branch/SKILL.md`）—— 集成、清理、提 PR。"

#: ../../source/chapters/08-superpowers.md:34 3c428b32b9404cb58584595540aa6f6c
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Each step is a skill the agent opts into (or is nudged into) via the `using-"
"superpowers` meta-skill. Anthropic's skills documentation "
"{cite}`anthropic2024skills` describes the mechanism; Superpowers is the most"
" complete public library of skills authored against it."
msgstr ""
"每一步都是智能体通过 `using-superpowers` 这条元技能 *选择* 进入（或被 *推* 进入）的一项技能。Anthropic 的 "
"skills 文档 {cite}`anthropic2024skills` 描述了这套机制；Superpowers "
"是迄今为止、针对这套机制最完整的公开技能库。"

#: ../../source/chapters/08-superpowers.md:39 0a5820c490b54bc4a3973c5b58a854df
msgid "§08.2 — A representative skill (≤ 20 lines)"
msgstr "§08.2 —— 一条代表性的技能（不超过 20 行）"

#: ../../source/chapters/08-superpowers.md:41 4f941cc60e034c0a879222f20b67e189
msgid ""
"The `test-driven-development/SKILL.md` file is the load-bearing one; it is "
"also the shortest. The excerpt below reproduces its core (with ellipses "
"marking omitted prose) and is quoted under the upstream licence:"
msgstr ""
"`test-driven-development/SKILL.md` "
"是承重的那一份，同时也是最短的一份。下面摘录了它的核心（用省略号标出省略的散文），并在上游许可证下引用："

#: ../../source/chapters/08-superpowers.md:46 9e0de79a110a49eeb692de8534378261
msgid ""
"# Test-Driven Development\n"
"\n"
"## When to use\n"
"\n"
"Use when implementing any feature or bugfix, before writing implementation code.\n"
"\n"
"## What this skill does\n"
"\n"
"1. Writes a failing test that captures the requirement.\n"
"2. Runs the test suite and confirms only this test fails.\n"
"3. Implements the minimum code to make the test pass.\n"
"4. Refactors while the test stays green.\n"
"\n"
"## Red flags that stop this skill\n"
"\n"
"- \"I'll write the test after.\" — no. The skill exits.\n"
"- A passing first test — suspect; re-read the requirement.\n"
msgstr ""
"# Test-Driven Development\n"
"\n"
"## When to use\n"
"\n"
"Use when implementing any feature or bugfix, before writing implementation code.\n"
"\n"
"## What this skill does\n"
"\n"
"1. Writes a failing test that captures the requirement.\n"
"2. Runs the test suite and confirms only this test fails.\n"
"3. Implements the minimum code to make the test pass.\n"
"4. Refactors while the test stays green.\n"
"\n"
"## Red flags that stop this skill\n"
"\n"
"- \"I'll write the test after.\" — no. The skill exits.\n"
"- A passing first test — suspect; re-read the requirement.\n"

#: ../../source/chapters/08-superpowers.md:66 fc5a015021de43b7ae750b6f5a4a98de
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"This is a skill file, *not* a code module — the agent's behaviour is changed"
" by reading prose, not by invoking an API. Mills' Socratic design essay "
"{cite}`mills2015socratic` and Zeller's systematic debugging "
"{cite}`zeller2009whyprogramsfail` are the intellectual ancestors: the skill "
"asks the agent to interrogate itself before committing to action."
msgstr ""
"这是一份技能文件，*不是* 一个代码模块——智能体的行为是靠读散文被改变的，而不是靠调用 API。Mills 的 Socratic design 论文 "
"{cite}`mills2015socratic`、以及 Zeller 的系统性调试 "
"{cite}`zeller2009whyprogramsfail`，是这类做法的思想先人：技能要求智能体在提交行动之前，先审问自己。"

#: ../../source/chapters/08-superpowers.md:72 17fda16b308546f79e414bdc5024c27f
msgid "§08.3 — OpenHarness vs Superpowers: complementary, not competing"
msgstr "§08.3 —— OpenHarness vs Superpowers：互补，不是竞争"

